  <!-- ================= About ================= -->
  <section class="sec" style="padding-top: 0" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <div class="wrap about" id="about">
      <div class="about-text rv">
        <p class="eyebrow">About the author</p>
        <div class="about-hello">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/img/ted.webp" type="image/webp">
            <img class="about-photo" src="/img/ted.jpg" width="600" height="600" alt="Ted Shachtman" loading="lazy">
          </picture>
          <h2 id="about-title">Hi, I’m Ted Shachtman</h2>
        </div>
        <p>I’m a teacher and software engineer with a deep interest in cognitive science. I have degrees in elementary education and cognitive studies from Vanderbilt University, and a master’s in computer science from the University of Colorado Boulder.</p>
        <p>I developed concept bubbles as a technique for learning and memory. I use it to remember lists, numbers, song lyrics and what people said, to learn board games, complex math and computer science, to play chess in my head, and to think through complex strategic problems. I made the animated lessons and started <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/MentalAtlas/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">r/MentalAtlas</a> so people can compare notes.</p>
        <p>I write up the techniques as essays on <a href="https://thoughtfeel.substack.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Substack</a>.</p>
        <p>thoughtfeel is the name of this site and of my company. The technique was first published under that name.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact rv">
        <h3>Get in touch</h3>
        <p>If you want to reach out about the technique, ask questions, or have a <strong>free tutoring session</strong>, please email me. I’d be very happy to jump on a call.</p>
        <p class="email" id="email-address">teddyshachtman@gmail.com</p>
        <div class="row">
          <a class="btn primary" href="mailto:teddyshachtman@gmail.com?subject=Concept%20bubbles">Email me</a>
          <button class="btn" type="button" id="copy-email">Copy address</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

